    "body": "## Change Summary\n\n- **What changed?**\n  - `--dataset-path` now accepts a **comma-separated list** of LeRobotV2 (v2.0/v2.1) dataset directories. A single path keeps the previous behaviour; multiple paths are concatenated.\n  - Added `MultiLeRobotV2Dataset` (`loongforge/embodied/data/datasets/lerobot_dataset.py`): concatenates N `LeRobotV2Dataset`s, each keeping its own `task_index -> text` map. `__len__` is the total frame count, so a uniform sampler yields **frame-count-weighted sampling** across suites.\n  - `build_fastwam_lerobot_dataset` (`.../fastwam/fastwam_dataset.py`) splits `--dataset-path` on commas and returns either the single dataset (unchanged path) or the multi-dataset wrapper.\n  - The wrapper propagates the dataloader-injected `_transform` to every sub-dataset and aggregates per-suite `stats` via `aggregate_stats` for normalization.\n- **Which issue or requirement does this address?**\n  - Reproduces the official FastWAM LIBERO \"4 suites joint\" training setup (spatial + object + goal + 10, frame-count-weighted). Previously impossible: the comma string was treated as one directory, raising `FileNotFoundError` on `<whole-string>/meta/episodes.jsonl`.\n- **Which modules are affected?**\n  - `data`, `vla` (embodied data path only).\n\n## Validation\n\n- [x] I ran the relevant local checks.\n- [ ] I added or updated tests where appropriate.\n- [x] I checked compatibility with existing APIs and configurations.\n\n## CI, GPU, and Image Impact\n\n- [ ] This change affects dependencies, Dockerfiles, patches, or runtime environments.\n- [ ] GPU validation is required. Suggested suite: `llm_vlm` / `embodied`.\n- [ ] A local candidate image should be built during GPU validation.\n- [x] No GPU or image validation is required.\n\n## Reviewer Notes\n\n- **Already exercised in a real FastWAM SFT run:** the comma-separated multi-suite path has been used for actual 4-suite joint SFT training (spatial + object + goal + 10), i.e. the data/training integration is validated in practice, not just by unit-level checks.\n- **Local checks done (CPU, real data):** 4 LIBERO suites load with one `LeRobotV2Dataset: root=...` log line each; `len(dataset) == 277,713 ==` sum of sub-lengths; `__getitem__` bisection returns bitwise-identical samples to the corresponding sub-dataset (incl. boundary indices); `_transform` propagates to all sub-datasets; `stats`/`meta.stats` aggregate and are non-empty; single-path / comma-path / whitespace-and-trailing-comma inputs all dispatch correctly. `ruff check` clean.\n- **Backward compatibility:** the change is additive. `LeRobotV2Dataset`/`LeRobotV3Dataset` are untouched; `build_fastwam_lerobot_dataset` is only used by the `fastwam` dataset strategy, and its single-path branch calls `_build_lerobot_dataset` with the same arguments as before. Other models that use the lerobot datasets (groot, pi05, xvla, ...) are unaffected.\n- **Scope / risks:**\n  - Covers LeRobotV2 (v2.0/v2.1) only; v3.0 is out of scope (upstream's `MultiLeRobotV3Dataset` is separate).\n  - Uses `episodes=None` (full dataset); per-root episode filtering is not supported yet.\n  - Assumes sub-datasets share the same `fps` / `chunks_size` semantics (holds for the LIBERO suites).\n- **Follow-up:** an optional unit test with a synthetic fixture (no real data dependency) was not added in this change.\n",
